      "content": "St. John's Wort is not safe to take with hormonal birth control due to a well-documented interaction that can cause the contraceptive to fail, regardless of the dose or how \"natural\" the herb appears. Even a low dose can significantly reduce hormone levels in your system without warning, leading to unpredictable pregnancy risks. For irregular medication interactions and seasonal mood issues, over-the-counter advice often isn't enough, so a quick consultation with a pharmacist or doctor is the only truly safe option.",
